WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Hello. I'm Mr. Red.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:37.000
Hello.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.160
I'd like to make a reservation.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.640
Is this Trans-Oceanic Airlines?

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.880
No, lady.

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:55.880
This is the Pony Express.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.560
Who was that on the phone?

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.760
Well, who was it?

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.760
Wrong number.

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.280
You know, you're a strange horse.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.280
You'll talk on the phone, you'll talk to me, but you won't talk in front of other people. Why?

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:11.200
How should I know?

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.680
I'm a horse, not a psychiatrist.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:20.160
Millions of horses in the world and I have to get the one who talks.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.600
Why do I only seem to hear voices when I come in here?

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.080
I want to ask you a favor.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.120
Sure, what is it?

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.200
Would you allow me to take your horse over to State University for the weekend?

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.000
I doubt if they'd accept him.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.280
He never got out of high school.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.840
No, really, I'm serious.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:40.120
You see, I attended an alumni meeting last night of Sigma Nu Delta.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.560
That's my old fraternity at State U.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:47.080
Well, it seems that State's rival college has stolen our mascot, a horse just like yours.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.680
And I promised the boys I would deliver Mr. Red for the big game next Saturday against Brighton U.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.200
Well, since you promised, you can't have him.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.440
Well, thank you...

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.200
I beg your pardon.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.160
Maybe you better get another horse.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.280
Ed is very uncomfortable away from home.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.920
But the university is only a ten minute drive from here and the boys will bring him back right after the game.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:11.600
Well, as long as they bring him back, you can't have him.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.840
Well, look, I'm in a bad spot.

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:18.360
I promised the boys the horse and you're putting me in a very difficult position.

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.920
Well, if that's the case, you're in trouble.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.520
I'm sorry, Roger.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.240
Well, that's quite all right.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:53.240
Thank you, neighbor.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.760
Yes?

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:57.000
Is Mr. Utterson there?

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.120
Nope.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:02:59.560
Who is this?

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.120
Willie McIntyre.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.840
Is this the man who's going to lend us the horse?

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:12.520
Get yourself a mule.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.600
Yes, I understand how important it is for you to borrow, Mr. Ed.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:21.000
You know, Carol, I've done a few favors for Wilbur, like getting him the contract to build Mr. Gordon's ranch house.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:21.880
I know.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:24.840
And the lawnmower, I lend him every Sunday.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:30.440
Of course, I'm not the kind who would remind Wilbur of these things, but I wish you would.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:32.760
I'll talk to him, Roger.

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:37.800
Sometimes I can get him to do things, especially if he thinks it's his idea.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.000
There he is. I'll call you.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:45.480
Oh.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:46.920
Who is that, honey?

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.840
That Roger Addison.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.360
I wish he'd stop pestering us about lending him Mr. Ed.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.520
He just doesn't give up, huh?

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.960
He's never done us any favors.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.120
Oh, let's be fair, honey.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:04.360
Well, name one thing.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.080
He got me the contract for the Gordon ranch house.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.280
What else?

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:09.560
Those theater tickets.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:11.080
What else?

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.920
Well, uh...

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:17.960
So he lends you his lawnmower every Sunday.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.560
Did I say that?

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:20.520
All right.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:24.600
If it means that much to you, lend Roger the horse.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:26.200
It would upset you, darling.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.160
Oh, no, no, no.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.120
You've convinced me.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.280
Lend Roger the horse.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.800
That's what I love about you.

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:56.360
When you're wrong, you admit it.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.720
Roger, listen.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:58.840
It worked.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:01.960
Oh, bless you, my dear.

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.960
I still don't understand why your husband raised

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.480
such a fuss over that old nag.

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:09.080
What was that?

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.400
Must be a bad connection.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:14.040
Well, thanks again, and goodbye, my dear.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:26.840
Ed, I've been thinking.

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.200
Not lately.

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.200
Ed, listen.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.600
Maybe you'd have fun being mascot for those kids,

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.640
just for the weekend.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:34.600
No, thanks.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.000
I'd rather die in bed.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.080
Well, you may get your picture in the paper.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:44.440
With 22 football players on my back.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.800
Look at it from my point of view.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.560
Mr. Addison is my neighbor.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:51.320
He's been doing me a lot of favors,

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:53.240
and it's about time I did him one.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:54.760
They tricked you, Wilbur.

00:05:54.760 --> 00:05:56.200
I heard him on the phone.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.040
Never mind what you heard on the phone.

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.920
I'm telling Mr. Addison the Sigma Nu Delta

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.760
can borrow you for the football game.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:05.820
Oh.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:08.760
Lay it on hard, lay it on low.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:10.760
All right, stay, stay.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:14.040
Go, go, go.

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:21.320
Why don't you watch where you're going?

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:22.360
I'm sorry.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:24.760
My name is Wilbur Post.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:27.320
I lent you fellas my horse for the football game.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.280
Football game.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.200
With an S and a T and an A-T-E.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.160
Stay, stay.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:31.660
Yay!

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:33.340
T.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.400
I know, fellas, but won't you even listen to me?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.400
Excuse me, I'm Wilbur Post.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.800
I lent you my horse for the football game.

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.000
I'm a little worried about him.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.360
It's his first time away from home.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:51.720
Would you boys know where they're keeping him?

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.720
You are fraternity boys, aren't you?

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:56.600
You are boys.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:06:59.720
You are alive.

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.120
Why should I want to fool you fellas?

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.360
I tell you, Norma's a living doll.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.040
She'll go nuts over him.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:21.560
Pardon me, my name is Wilbur Post.

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.600
I'm here about my horse.

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:24.440
Would you know where they've hidden him?

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.640
I'll call you right back, fellas.

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.920
Are you a spy from Brighton?

00:07:37.400 --> 00:07:40.120
Now, fellas, please, you've got this all wrong.

00:07:40.120 --> 00:07:43.160
I'm Wilbur Post, Mr. Addison's friend.

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.520
I'm the one who lent you the horse.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:46.520
I just want to see him.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:50.520
Oh, well, we've got him hidden where those Brighton creeps won't find him.

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.160
Oh, well, would you mind telling me where?

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.320
Hi, Hank.

00:08:01.320 --> 00:08:02.200
How's our horse?

00:08:05.800 --> 00:08:07.480
I think he likes it in that steam room.

00:08:07.480 --> 00:08:09.480
We better not keep him in there too long.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.000
He's liable to come out a pony.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.280
Willie, you're a genius for dreaming this up.

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.840
Those BU guys will never think of looking for him in here.

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:19.240
The horse's owner is coming over now to have a look at him.

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:20.760
It's okay to let him in.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:21.260
Check.

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:24.360
Uh-oh, here comes Professor Thornhill.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:25.320
What do we do?

00:08:25.320 --> 00:08:26.360
Don't panic.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:27.880
I'll handle him.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.280
Ah, MacIntyre.

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.240
Hi, River.

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.440
How's the steam today?

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:35.640
Nice and warm, I hope?

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.040
Oh, Professor, it's pretty hot in there.

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:39.800
Maybe you ought to skip it today.

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:41.480
The heat's liable to crack your glasses.

00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.040
Oh, I always leave my glasses outside.

00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:44.540
Ah!

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:49.080
Oh, dear, oh, dear.

00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:50.700
Oh!

00:08:57.880 --> 00:08:58.840
Now, off we go.

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:09.400
Who's that big fellow in there?

00:09:10.120 --> 00:09:12.600
Uh, that's Moose Jackson, sir.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:14.440
You better not go in there, sir.

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.840
He's still sore at you because you flunked him in psychology.

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:18.120
Oh, I had to fail him.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:21.080
In his last examination, he even spelt his name wrong.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.800
Oh, I beg your pardon.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:33.180
Here.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:38.940
I'm so sorry.

00:09:49.420 --> 00:09:52.460
Gentlemen, there is a horse in the steam room.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:53.340
A horse, sir?

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:54.140
Yes, a horse.

00:09:54.140 --> 00:09:55.580
And don't tell me it's the moose.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.180
Well, sir, that horse is our new mascot, sir.

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.940
We were hiding him from the BU guys.

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:03.100
MacIntyre, what are you majoring in?

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.060
Physics, sir.

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:04.700
Oliver?

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.980
Advanced electronics, sir.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:11.980
And to think, the free world is waiting for you scientists.

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:29.340
Ed, I've been looking.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:32.860
Oh, sorry, sir, I thought you were someone else.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.220
Oh, it's quite all right.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:40.060
Tell me, young man, you always wear all your clothes in the steam room?

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:46.220
Well, I... I have a cold.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:51.420
Oh, I see. That probably makes sense.

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:59.260
By the way, by the way, have you noticed that we have two

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.060
horses in that company?

00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:04.300
Nobody here, sir, just us and the horse.

00:11:05.580 --> 00:11:07.340
Just us and the horse.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:12.220
Tell me, young man, are you majoring in any science?

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:13.740
No, sir.

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.140
Oh, then there is hope for the world.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.740
Ed, it's good to see you.

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:26.860
How are you, boy?

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:29.260
Medium rare.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:33.500
Cheer up. He'll find another hiding place for you.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.380
By tomorrow, they'll have me up on a church steeple.

00:11:38.140 --> 00:11:40.380
Come on, enjoy yourself while you're here.

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:41.500
Have fun with the kids.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:43.740
Hit them hard, hit them low.

00:11:43.740 --> 00:11:45.820
Come on, steak, go, go, go.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:48.540
My life is at stake in your cheering.

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:51.980
I'm sorry about this, Ed.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.260
I'll make it up to you later.

00:11:53.260 --> 00:11:58.700
Just keep the services dignified and simple.

00:11:58.700 --> 00:11:59.820
You're not angry with me, are you?

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:03.580
I'll see you at the game.

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:05.340
Wilbur.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:05.740
Yeah?

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.260
Close the door fast.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:23.740
These drafts are murder.

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:41.740
By tomorrow, they'll have me up on a church steeple.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:13:01.740
My life is at stake in your cheering.

00:13:11.900 --> 00:13:29.420
Just keep the services dignified and simple.

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:31.820
Wilbur.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.220
Honey, you ate so little at dinner.

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:37.740
I fixed a little snack for you.

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:38.380
Thank you, dear.

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:41.340
Oh, darling, you're not still worried about Mr. Ed, are you?

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:42.380
No, of course not.

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:42.940
Wilbur.

00:13:43.660 --> 00:13:44.460
Wilbur.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:46.140
Wilbur, here they are.

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:48.460
Four tickets on the 50-yard line.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.140
Oh, Roger, you shouldn't have bought them.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:51.100
I didn't buy them.

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:53.340
They're a gift from the Sigma Nu Delta boys.

00:13:53.340 --> 00:13:53.980
Pretty good, huh?

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:58.380
If I find him up on a church steeple, it's all your fault.

00:13:58.380 --> 00:13:59.900
Church steeple?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.860
What are you talking about?

00:14:02.860 --> 00:14:03.660
Oh, nothing.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:11.180
I'll get it.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:11.660
Hello?

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:13.340
Yes, he's here.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:14.140
Who?

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:17.900
One of the boys from the fraternity, Willie McIntyre.

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:18.540
Let me take that.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:20.620
Hello?

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:23.980
I've got some bad news for you about your horse.

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:25.020
Bad news?

00:14:25.020 --> 00:14:25.820
What happened to him?

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:28.060
That bunch from Brighton jumped us and stole him.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.020
What's wrong, dear?

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:30.780
Mr. Ed.

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:33.980
Mr. Ed's been stolen.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:43.180
Wilbur.

00:14:43.180 --> 00:14:43.900
Hello, Edna?

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:47.180
Our boys did it to state you again.

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:50.380
We've got their first mascot hidden at a riding academy.

00:14:50.380 --> 00:14:52.380
I'm sure they'll be happy to see you.

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:53.180
I'm sure they'll be.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:53.980
I'm sure they'll be.

00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:54.780
I'm sure they'll be.

00:14:54.780 --> 00:14:55.580
I'm sure they'll be.

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:56.380
I'm sure they'll be.

00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:57.180
I'm sure they'll be.

00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:58.780
I'm sure they'll be.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:00.460
And guess where the second one is?

00:15:01.180 --> 00:15:03.420
Right in the basement of our sorority house.

00:15:10.140 --> 00:15:11.180
Good evening, Sandy.

00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:18.380
Hello, Mrs. Davis.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:25.420
Linda, how did the boys ever get the horse out of that steam room?

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:27.340
Weren't there any state boys guarding him?

00:15:28.060 --> 00:15:29.260
It was a breeze.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:30.300
I was a decoy.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:34.300
You mean they sent you into the steam room?

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:36.620
Don't be ridiculous, Gloria.

00:15:36.620 --> 00:15:41.100
One of the boys told the boy guarding the steam room that a blonde wanted to see him outside.

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.220
And he left his post?

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:45.980
Honey, when he saw me, he would have left his country.

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:50.540
And what did you do to keep him outside while our boys were stealing the horse?

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:54.700
Well, we discussed the international situation.

00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:59.180
Girls, girls, hold it down.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:00.940
Mrs. Davis just came back.

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:04.460
If she finds out the horse is right down here in the basement, we're in trouble.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:06.860
Do you think Mrs. Davis suspects anything?

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.060
Not so far.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:11.420
She'd been so busy fixing up the house for Miss Pentecost's lecture.

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:13.420
And what a subject for a lecture.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:14.940
Ornithology.

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:16.060
That's for the birds.

00:16:17.260 --> 00:16:19.100
Oh, poor horse.

00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:20.860
He must be hungry.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.980
Let's fix him some poached eggs or something.

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:24.700
Great idea.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.580
Poached eggs.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:47.980
There it is.

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:48.860
Operator.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:49.820
Hello, honey.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:54.860
Will you get me state 11781?

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:56.780
You can dial that number, sir.

00:16:56.780 --> 00:16:57.580
Dialing number.

00:16:57.580 --> 00:16:59.580
You can dial that number, sir.

